        "timestamp": 1792488723
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> ilyas-mallah submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14883#pullrequestreview-5584072212\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 633278826,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792493757
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> ilyas-mallah created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14883#discussion_r4324172993\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The guard is needed because <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/fa20b4c09b3002afb1b20eb5a3385c28a4290d63/cranelift/codegen/src/isa/s390x/inst.isle#L4930-L4937\"><code>fpromote_reg</code></a> isn't <code>partial</code>. A pair it has no rule for panics instead of being rejected. On main, <code>clif-util compile --target s390x</code> of <code>fpromote.f64</code> on an f16 value exits 101 with \"no rule matched for term fpromote_reg ... should it be partial?\". The new s390x filetest fails on main with that panic.</p>\n<p>The old generic rule sent every f16 pair into the helper, so the explicit pairs keep f16 out of it. I can make the two helpers partial instead. That touches 19 call sites in lower.isle, which would each need to handle a missing match. Do you prefer that?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633278829,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792493757
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> ilyas-mallah submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14883#pullrequestreview-5584072515\">PR review</a>.</p>",
